    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33126" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ōsor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossor</span></b> ,
		Plaut. l. l. infra), ōris, m.
		odi, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				hater</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uxoris suae ossor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					As. 5, 2, 9</span></i>
			 Fleck. (Ussing, osor): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. de Deo Socr. p. 48, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pacat. Pan. Th. 20, 5</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4, 24</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulierum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. prol. 74</span></i>
			; cf.: osorem dixerunt, qui aliquem odisset, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				196</span></i> Müll.</div>
